# HTTP and HTTPS — IT 3203 Milestone 1

Author: Deborah Daramola
Topic: The Evolution of HTTP and HTTPS

## Open locally
Extract the ZIP into a folder, then open index.html in a browser. All navigation and images use relative paths. No build, JavaScript, external CSS, framework, or package installation is required.

## Files
- index.html — abstract, key terms, and table of contents
- evolution.html — HTTP history, version table, and browser exercise
- https.html — TLS, certificates, and limits of connection security
- concepts.html — seven key concepts
- references.html — technical sources and learning resources
- about.html — author introduction and project purpose
- styles.css — the only stylesheet
- assets/ — two original, accessible SVG illustrations

## GitHub Pages publication (required for course submission)
1. Sign in to GitHub and create a dedicated repository, for example it3203-http-evolution.
2. Upload the extracted website files to the repository ROOT. index.html should sit at the top level, with styles.css and assets/ alongside it. Do not upload only the ZIP or an extra enclosing folder.
3. Open repository Settings > Pages. Under Build and deployment, choose Deploy from a branch, then main and /(root). Save.
4. Wait for GitHub to publish the site, then use the URL displayed in Pages settings. For a standard project site it is usually https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/it3203-http-evolution/.
5. Open that URL, check all six pages and both images, and submit the working clickable link in the D2L comment box. Attach this source ZIP as required.

These instructions follow GitHub’s “Creating a GitHub Pages site” guide:
https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/creating-a-github-pages-site
Repository visibility and Pages availability depend on the GitHub account’s plan and policies.

## Requirement map
- Six pages with identical main navigation and current-page indication.
- Home page contains a title, abstract, key terms, and linked contents.
- Two research pages, references, seven concepts, and an About page.
- Headings, lists, images with alternatives, and an accessible comparison table.
- One CSS file. Element selectors: body, h1, table. Class selectors: .site-header, .note. ID selector: #main.
- Flexbox for a basic wrapping navigation menu; single-column content.
- Link hover and focus effects, margins, padding, borders, colors, and font settings.
- HTML/CSS comments, class-project footer, and the course link.
- Basic narrow-screen styling.

Review and personalize the About page and understand the source before submitting. The simple design uses a blue header, a white content area, standard headings, and basic borders. It uses no copied site template or whole-site framework. GitHub Pages publication is a separate final step because this package is not connected to your GitHub account.
